Subject: Modeling Algorithms - BRepOffset_MakeOffset visits arc-join offset faces in the order they were bound
Upstream: https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT/pull/1600 (author: gsdali; open as of 2026-10-07)
Applies to: OCCT V7_9_3, backported from the PR (written for 8.0): 7.9.3's iterator over the
     offset map is BRepOffset_DataMapIteratorOfDataMapOfShapeOffset, otherwise the change is
     the same. Source change only; the PR's GTest file targets IR and is left out.
Why: BuildOffsetByArc iterated a map hashed by TShape address, so the face order of every
     arc-join offset (and the last bits of its volume) changed from run to run. With this patch
     the experiment's 605-case stress test is bit-identical across runs and platforms.
Drop when: Silico upgrades to an OCCT release that includes PR #1600 (or upstream's equivalent).

--- a/src/BRepOffset/BRepOffset_MakeOffset.cxx
+++ b/src/BRepOffset/BRepOffset_MakeOffset.cxx
@@ -1925,6 +1925,23 @@
   {
     return;
   }
+  // MapSF is hashed on TShape addresses. Visit its entries in the order they were bound,
+  // otherwise the roots of myImageOffset, and so the faces of the result, change from run to run.
+  NCollection_IndexedMap<TopoDS_Shape, TopTools_ShapeMapHasher> aBindOrder;
+  {
+    // The order MakeOffsetFaces binds the faces in.
+    NCollection_List<TopoDS_Shape> aSortedFaces;
+    BRepLib::SortFaces(myFaceComp, aSortedFaces);
+    for (NCollection_List<TopoDS_Shape>::Iterator anIt(aSortedFaces); anIt.More(); anIt.Next())
+    {
+      aBindOrder.Add(anIt.Value());
+    }
+    for (NCollection_List<TopoDS_Shape>::Iterator anIt(myAnalyse.NewFaces()); anIt.More();
+         anIt.Next())
+    {
+      aBindOrder.Add(anIt.Value());
+    }
+  }
